      "note": "DiGiCo S-Series User Guide issue J (S21 and S31), opened 2026-11-12: rear-panel figure labels mic/line inputs (24), line outputs (12), AES I/O, word clock I/O, GPI/O, console Ethernet, DVI, UB MADI USB, console USB, two DMI card slots; the power switch is on the rear panel; 21 motorised 100 mm faders and two multi-touch screens. DiGiCo documents no connector TYPE and no size for this model (the brochure link of the plan is dead); the dealer page names XLR, BNC, RJ-45 and an IEC inlet and its counts disagree with the manual (Ethernet, word clock, AES, USB), so the connector set is not documented: beta-modelled, 8 of 24 mic inputs and 4 of 12 outputs as a stand-in. Size 763 x 586 x 295 mm, 19 kg is dealer-only (Sonovente). Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, faders, knobs and screens drawn without lettering, no photo, no logo. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess) and the side profile is an estimate drawn from the three outer sizes (no drawing opened). Connector genders not stated by the source follow the convention input = female, output = male."
